00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:50.960
Pop the hood on multi turn image editing and the key mechanism reuses latent representations from earlier steps while injecting noise only into changed regions.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:06:07.540
That targeted approach cuts compute by roughly 60 to 70% compared with full regeneration from scratch. A lightweight subject encoder extracts identity tokens once and feeds them at every denoising step adding 15 to 25 milliseconds per iteration.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:21.780
The consistency gain holds only when reference images stay inside a narrow distribution out of domain subjects lose fidelity unless the encoder is rerun or the attention mask is tightened, which removes the latency savings.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:31.680
Builders therefore choose this path for repeated design iterations and switch to single shot generation when the subject or style shifts dramatically between turns.

